From dd6023d2b29e3d1da3390f69a06c869c1b9b033e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:10:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rpcd: apps_std: support writing files in mapped
 directories

The sensors registry on OnePlus 9 Pro (SM8350) saves groups by writing
temp.json and renaming it into place. With fopen("w") refused, the SLPI
retries every ~20 ms for ~40 s before sensors come up.

Add fwrite, fsync, fremove, ftrunc and frename, and allow fopen_with_env
in "w"/"a" modes. Only mapped directories implement the new create and
fileno ops, so virtual directories stay read-only and physical
permissions decide what the DSP may change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
